doctype html
html
  head
    //- Interpolation syntax
    title Natours-2025 | #{guess}
    meta(charset="utf-8")
    meta(name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0")
    link(rel="stylesheet" href="/css/style.css")
    link(rel="shortcut icon" type='image/png'  href="img/favicon.png")
  body
    h1 Welcome to Natours-2025 - Server-Side Rendering with Pug!
    h2 Welcome #{user.name}!
    h2= guess.toUpperCase()
    // Line above is called buffered code!
    // Visible comment in Devtools!
    //- Invisible comment in Devtools!
    // And unbuffered code
    - const x = 9;
    h2= 10 * x / 9 
    //- = 10
    br
    p This is a simple Pug template with dynamic data.
    br
    ul When a user visits /, Express + Pug:
    li 1. Fetch the template.
    li 2. Insert any data, it will pass res.render('base', { tour })).
    li 3. Compile it into real HTML.
    li 4. Send the complete HTML page to the browser.
    br
    p The browser then simply renders the DOM immediately, because it already has a full HTML page from the backend.
    br
    h3 Your upcoming tours:
    ul
      each tour in tours
        li #{tour.name} - $#{tour.price} - Duration: #{tour.duration} days

    if tours.length === 0
      p You have no upcoming tours.
